etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4173101\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: thestar.com.my\nSLUG: motor-racing-title-to-lose-antonelli-set-for-f1-history-either-way\nTEXT: Kimi Antonelli is either on track to become Formula One\'s youngest world champion or will be the first driver to win five races in a row without taking the title. The 19-year-old Italian\'s dominant run at Monaco, where he mastered the streets and set the fastest lap, has moved him 66 points clear of Lewis Hamilton in the championship standings. Antonelli\'s teammate George Russell, who has failed to score for two successive races, is now 68 points behind and faces an uphill battle to catch up. Team boss Toto Wolff believes Russell will come back strong, but history is against him as only 10 drivers have won five races in a row since the championship started in 1950, and none of them did so without going on to win the title.\n\nID: 4172562\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: title-lose-antonelli-set-f1-history-either-way-6169596\nTEXT: Kimi Antonelli has set a record for either being the youngest Formula One world champion before the end of the season or winning five consecutive races in a single campaign. His dominant run at Monte Carlo, where he started from pole and set the fastest lap, has moved him 66 points clear of Lewis Hamilton in the championship standings. Antonelli\'s lead over Hamilton is 68 points, while he also holds a significant advantage over Mercedes teammate George Russell, who failed to score for the second consecutive race.\n\n\n',)
