etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4172641\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: nba-finals-trump-knicks-new-york-7b43bea56ff57b48f72d365efd1b7ddb\nTEXT: Donald Trump, a sitting U.S. president, will attend Game 3 of the NBA Finals between the New York Knicks and San Antonio Spurs at Madison Square Garden. Strict security measures have been put in place, requiring fans to arrive two hours early and pass through multiple checkpoints, including a TSA-style magnetometer. The New York Police Department and Secret Service have established a multi-block security perimeter around the arena, canceling a watch party outside and implementing a no-bag policy for ticket-holders. Police Commissioner Jessica Tisch stated that the decision was made to support Trump\'s visit, but acknowledged that New Yorkers are accustomed to presidential visits resulting in lockdowns of areas.\n\nID: 4173013\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: koat.com\nSLUG: 71527685\nTEXT: President Donald Trump will attend Game 3 of the NBA Finals on Monday, where he\'ll watch the New York Knicks face the San Antonio Spurs. The Secret Service is increasing security measures in and around Madison Square Garden due to Trump\'s attendance, with a larger deployment of NYPD officers both above ground and below ground. The Secret Service aims to ensure a safe experience for attendees, with a focus on protecting Trump as the first sitting president to attend an NBA Finals game.\n\n\n',)
