etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4172995\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: koat.com\nSLUG: 71525483\nTEXT: Brendan Sorsby, a 22-year-old quarterback at Texas Tech, has been granted a temporary injunction against the NCAA, allowing him to potentially play for the team this fall. The injunction was granted after Sorsby\'s lawsuit, filed May 18, sought the restoration of his eligibility. The NCAA had previously denied Sorsby\'s request to reinstate his eligibility, citing a betting scandal involving the quarterback. Judge Ken Curry ruled that the NCAA cannot block Sorsby\'s eligibility, citing a diagnosed addiction and anxiety-driven compulsion. This decision could clear the way for Sorsby to play for Texas Tech, despite being declared ineligible due to wagering on college sports.\n\nID: 4173152\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: deseret.com\nSLUG: brendan-sorsby-gets-injunction-vs-ncaa-could-play-for-texas-tech-this-fall\nTEXT: Brendan Sorsby, a 22-year-old quarterback, has received an injunction in his lawsuit against the NCAA. The case centers on Sorsby\'s eligibility to play for Texas Tech this fall, following an NCAA investigation. Sorsby has a diagnosed addiction and anxiety-driven compulsion, which his attorney, Jeffrey Kessler, claims would be exacerbated by not playing football. In contrast, the NCAA maintains that it must defend against actions that defraud college athletics and threaten competitive integrity. The injunction allows Sorsby to play for Texas Tech this fall, pending further appeals by the NCAA.\n\n\n',)
