etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4171951\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: defensenews.com\nSLUG: germany-and-france-drop-joint-fighter-jet-project\nTEXT: Germany and France have dropped their joint fighter jet project, a €100-billion ($116 billion) endeavor. The decision was made after German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and French President Emmanuel Macron discussed the project on the sidelines of the EU-Western Balkans summit in Montenegro. The two sides failed to reach an agreement on specifications and control, leading to a deadlock that couldn\'t be broken. The project\'s core fighter jet, supported by drones and linked by a classified "combat cloud," will maintain the same name: Future Combat Air System or FCAS, in a face-saving solution.\n\nID: 4173266\nCREATED: 2026-06-09\nDOMAIN: politico.eu\nSLUG: berlin-declares-france-germany-next-gen-fighter-jet-project-dead\nTEXT: Germany and France have effectively ended their joint Next-Generation Fighter Jet project, FCAS. The two countries had agreed to give the multibillion-euro program one last chance in March, but talks failed to overcome deep differences. The project\'s future is uncertain as the remaining partners - Germany, Italy, and Spain - consider how to proceed. The end of the fighter aircraft component was not a sudden rupture, but rather the result of a slow and grinding fight between Airbus and Dassault Aviation, two of Europe\'s most influential defense contractors.\n\n\n',)
