etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4172802\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: ocregister.com\nSLUG: earthquake-with-6-1-magnitude-hits-offshore-cuba-shaking-buildings-in-havana\nTEXT: A 6.1 magnitude earthquake struck near western Cuba on Monday, shaking buildings in Havana and beyond. The quake occurred at a depth of six miles in waters just west of the capital, according to the U.S. Geological Survey. Flavia Pupo, a manager at the Pinar del Río hotel in Pinar del Río, described how the building shook and caused some fear. "Everyone here is OK," she said by telephone, noting that the people on the street are a little bit scared. The latest earthquake was felt as far away as Florida, with reports of shaking in the southwestern part of the state.\n\nID: 4172856\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: cbs8.com\nSLUG: 507-3ebfe0f9-6c3e-48a7-854e-28dc1eebfd83\nTEXT: An earthquake was felt in Florida after a 5.7-magnitude quake struck near Cuba, according to reports. The earthquake occurred at approximately 10:30 am local time in the Caribbean Sea, about 90 miles east of Cuba\'s coast. Florida residents reported feeling the quake, with some describing it as a strong jolt. The US Geological Survey (USGS) confirmed the earthquake, stating that it was centered near Cuba but felt in southern Florida.\n\nID: 4172015\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: news18.com\nSLUG: 6-1-magnitude-earthquake-strikes-cuba-tremors-felt-across-parts-of-florida-ws-l-10137413-html\nTEXT: A 6.1-magnitude earthquake struck western Cuba near Mantua, causing tremors to be felt across parts of Florida. Residents in cities such as Miami and Orlando reported experiencing mild shaking, with some describing movements in homes and offices. The quake struck at a depth of 10 kilometres (6.2 miles), making it shallow enough for tremors to be felt over a wide area, with no reports of major damage or injuries in Florida.\n\n\n',)
