etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4171377\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: prnewswire.com\nSLUG: awi-investors-have-opportunity-to-join-armstrong-world-industries-inc-fraud-investigation-with-the-schall-law-firm-302793482-html\nTEXT: The Schall Law Firm is investigating Armstrong World Industries Inc for potential securities law violations. The investigation centers on whether the company issued false or misleading statements, and/or failed to disclose pertinent information to investors. Following Armstrong\'s Q4 and full-year 2025 financial results, shares fell by about 10% on the same day. The company reported softer-than-expected volumes and a lack of normal bounce-back after reopening, which may have misled investors. Shareholders who suffered losses are encouraged to participate in the investigation and can contact Brian Schall of the Schall Law Firm at 310-301-3335 for a free consultation.\n\nID: 4171381\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: prnewswire.com\nSLUG: bmi-investors-have-opportunity-to-lead-badger-meter-inc-securities-fraud-lawsuit-with-the-schall-law-firm-302793485-html\nTEXT: A class action lawsuit has been filed against Badger Meter, Inc. (NYSE: BMI) for securities fraud. Investors who purchased the company\'s securities between April 18, 2024 and April 16, 2026, are encouraged to contact the Schall Law Firm before August 3, 2026. The firm claims that Badger Meter made false and misleading statements about its financial performance, citing "secular growth drivers" and "solid operating execution." However, the company\'s statements were actually based on pulling forward customer orders to recognize revenue early. The lawsuit alleges that these false statements caused investors to suffer damages when the truth came out.\n\n\n',)
