etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4171724\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: emirates247.com\nSLUG: 2358\nTEXT: Retail investors can buy SpaceX IPO shares through platforms like Fidelity Investments ($2,000), Robinhood Markets ($0), and SoFi ($0). However, brokerage requirements vary widely. International investors face varying regulations and eligibility criteria in countries such as Germany, France, Spain, Sweden, and the Netherlands. Investors may be able to participate once regulatory approvals are completed.\n\nBuyers who miss out on the IPO can still purchase SpaceX shares after listing, but share price volatility is expected due to demand exceeding supply. Large IPOs often see a sharp rise in price on the first day of trading, as investors compete for limited availability. Investors may also gain indirect exposure through index funds like the Nasdaq 100, which has included SpaceX following its listing.\n\nDespite strong demand, analysts caution that SpaceX\'s valuation relies heavily on sustained future growth. The company operates in a capital-intensive sector, where performance can be influenced by launch schedules, satellite deployment, and regulatory developments. SpaceX has indicated in its IPO prospectus that profitability is not expected in the near term.\n\nThe company is unlikely to meet the criteria for inclusion in the S&P 500 in the short term, as the index requires consistent profitability. Competition from other technology companies preparing to go public, along with share sales following lock-up periods, could place pressure on the stock price over time.\n\nID: 4170657\nCREATED: 2026-06-08\nDOMAIN: businessinsider.com\nSLUG: spacex-ipo-draws-investor-demand-of-150b-reuters-says-1036230980\nTEXT: SpaceX\'s highly anticipated IPO has drawn an unprecedented investor demand of $150B, more than double its initial target of $75B. According to Reuters, citing individuals familiar with the matter, Isla Binnie and Echo Wang reported this significant interest.\n\n\n',)
